      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\ud83d\udcca SGLT2 Inhibitors vs. GLP-1 Receptor Agonists for Type 2 Diabetes"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "While Metformin remains a standard first-line oral medication for many, modern guidelines prioritize choosing SGLT2 inhibitors or GLP-1 receptor agonists early\u2014or even as co-first-line options\u2014based on individual organ protection, weight goals, and underlying conditions.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Metformin",
            "link": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/type-2-diabetes/diagnosis-treatment/drc-20351199"
          }
        ],
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "modern guidelines prioritize choosing SGLT2 inhibitors or GLP-1 receptor agonists early\u2014or even as co-first-line options\u2014based on individual organ protection, weight goals, and underlying conditions"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Neither class is universally \"superior\"; instead, they target different clinical profiles.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          4,
